[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: laptop0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: host routing on Laptop0 (VLAN 20). The laptop’s default gateway is misconfigured.

Mechanism: Traffic to anything outside 172.16.20.0/24 is sent to the default next-hop 172.16.20.99 on eth0. ARP for this next-hop fails (“FAILED”), so the kernel cannot resolve a L2 destination and immediately returns “Destination Host Unreachable.” In-VLAN traffic (172.16.20.0/24) still works because it is directly connected and does not require a gateway.

Localization and evidence:
- On laptop0, ip route shows “default via 172.16.20.99 dev eth0” while the connected subnet is 172.16.20.0/24 (src 172.16.20.10).
- ip neigh shows “172.16.20.99 dev eth0 FAILED” and “172.16.20.1 … REACHABLE.” Pinging 172.16.20.99 fails; pinging 172.16.20.1 succeeds.
- router0 (the inter-VLAN router) has subinterface eth0.20 configured as 172.16.20.1/24, confirming the correct gateway for VLAN 20 is 172.16.20.1.
- Pings from laptop0 to off-VLAN hosts (e.g., 172.16.10.4) return “From 172.16.20.10 Destination Host Unreachable,” consistent with a bad default route rather than a network-wide routing issue.

Root cause: Laptop0’s default route points to a nonexistent gateway (172.16.20.99) instead of 172.16.20.1.

Corrective fix: On laptop0, replace the default route with “ip route del default; ip route add default via 172.16.20.1 dev eth0” and/or correct the persistent network/DHCP configuration so the default gateway is 172.16.20.1. After this change, inter-VLAN and external reachability should be restored. 
=== END ===